game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd226916-bde7-517b-871e-7e8629dd5812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550887} :answer-field/id #uuid "5784eef9-0ad2-5040-8dd4-135f8ec74797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d6dbf98c-84c4-5c67-a15a-4f405cbbd0b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-41401" :question/problem "The height (in feet) and the average number of points scored per game (APG) of four players on a basketball team are shown in the following table. \n\n| Height $(x)$ | **$6$** | **$6.5$** | **$6.5$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| APG $(y)$ | $5$ | $8$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft}?$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}84.75 & -13 \\\\ -13 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}33 \\\\ 217\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{X}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}^{\\beta } & =\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}^{y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}84.75 & -13 \\\\ -13 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}33 \\\\ 217\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24.25 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the line $y=-24.25+5x.$ \n\nFinally, to predict the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft},$  we substitute $x=6.45$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-24.25+5(6.45) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, according to the model,  the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft}$ will be $8$  points per game."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa5bf185-de29-5185-ba57-c64250332dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Polynomial Regression Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550604} {:answer/id #uuid "65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-5)^{2} \\\\ (-25)^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2} \\\\ {20}^{2} \\\\ {35}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550618} {:answer/id #uuid "a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1