edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "637f51dc-9306-5135-a973-8a82796a3f19" :question/math-academy-id "q-139809" :question/problem "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$-2$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$15$** | **$19$** | **$25$** | **$17$** | **$32$** |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-8$ | $-3$ | $6$ | $13$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the plane $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using multi linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$-2$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$15$** | **$19$** | **$25$** | **$17$** | **$32$** |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-8$ | $-3$ | $6$ | $13$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 15 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 19 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 25 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 17 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 32\\end{aligned}]}^{X}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}^{\\beta } & =\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]}^{y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c02160-8ba1-5939-bc73-8002657c6b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557912} {:answer/id #uuid "23f077b2-98bc-5e17-b96a-87b4b7d0879e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557942} {:answer/id #uuid "6de90c59-9c12-5214-92b7-f0abb8a7ca70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558082} {:answer/id #uuid "cadf1f12-7d08-5b35-add1-a8807ac05198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558272} {:answer/id #uuid "fade0afc-801b-5fae-b3a9-b016601c272f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fade0afc-801b-5fae-b3a9-b016601c272f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558358} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4f155d4-3ea5-53d0-a6f6-8b69b1f92207" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "758b84b6-7328-584d-83ee-1df88702770d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107500" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{L}\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,\\underbrace{(LU)}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL\\underbrace{(Ux)}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=4 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=4$ and ${y}_{2}=5.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=5$ and ${x}_{1}=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3+5=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14beea86-f47c-5a8c-9bec-dff707ad6098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557916} {:answer/id #uuid "2e855c15-8cb8-5eb3-ad1a-06b9a164a41f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557963} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb700b3-de35-5eef-a9b9-8f936285f7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558175} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd0b1f6-0564-5713-91c8-8b44037f4570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558178} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fda1e6-ea2c-5685-8e6d-c69133ac2877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dd0b1f6-0564-5713-91c8-8b44037f4570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558178} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d3d84a-5d38-5708-8891-cf429ce55b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "772e6d55-2cc0-5849-b50b-b1451b60fe6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-107185" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,\\underbrace{(LU)}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL\\underbrace{(Ux)}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 8{y}_{1}-5{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-3+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-3+2(-1) \\\\  & =-5, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =8-8{y}_{1}+5{y}_{2} \\\\  & =8-8(-1)+5(-5) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59687fe-7fee-536b-ae53-62aa4e2062c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59687fe-7fee-536b-ae53-62aa4e2062c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda1e7e4-3c88-5a06-909e-308c1b22da65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81eb1113-b696-53f5-ab1f-005ae9690189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81eb1113-b696-53f5-ab1f-005ae9690189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc834a44-d315-5323-8d37-5104d3268aa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a3f4d85-0623-5fd9-9cc9-8c8eac44c1ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-334846" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\underbrace{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+\\underbrace{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa5bf185-de29-5185-ba57-c64250332dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Polynomial Regression Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088f31e3-f49b-508d-9b4f-3b50e9543366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557885} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3876e4-0be8-5285-af5a-7c1a626b5415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 13 & {13}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -4 & (-4)^{2} \\\\ 1 & -18 & (-18)^{2} \\\\ 1 & -10 & (-10)^{2} \\\\ 1 & 11 & {11}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557893} {:answer/id #uuid "6b09ea0f-5f4a-5921-ae4b-58da76e0f97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 13 & {13}^{2} & {13}^{3} \\\\ 1 & -4 & (-4)^{2} & (-4)^{3} \\\\ 1 & -18 & (-18)^{2} & (-18)^{3} \\\\ 1 & -10 & (-10)^{2} & (-10)^{3} \\\\ 1 & 11 & {11}^{2} & {11}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558074} {:answer/id #uuid "9bda7b77-5680-5912-9bae-2e271d090576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ -4 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ -18 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ -10 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 11 & 8 & {8}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558172} {:answer/id #uuid "d015b672-4778-52e8-bb4e-468671c0d33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} & {6}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2} & {8}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "088f31e3-f49b-508d-9b4f-3b50e9543366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557885} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cd99673-6502-5535-8b37-2664b2ceabf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 