ht=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}} </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\underbrace{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+\\underbrace{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119884 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c159d750-ab1f-538b-b8cc-ae66ef1ae414" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix U of an LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a7fdb4-2b1b-532b-85f0-f8df64e8691a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557917} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4dfd2e-6508-5fbd-9bc5-a8e2a4a7b39d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557928} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfb90a2-2e70-5671-9927-bd4cc934f12d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557929} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4b5b3e-ad7c-5cf1-918a-e39ed5f2a6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558016} {:answer/id #uuid "c77be089-5efb-5143-95d8-be5cfb388426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c77be089-5efb-5143-95d8-be5cfb388426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558264} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c7a758e-cf09-5976-8b76-1ff485bab836" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "daed3fa2-ebc7-5729-abaf-5914fd69e7b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-106962" :question/problem "$$\n\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 28 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -49 & 37 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{A}=\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{L}\\cdot \\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}]}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 28 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -49 & 37 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -49 & 37 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${u}_{33}=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea7e0be-9a1f-5523-b787-ed5f453051d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557964} {:answer/id #uuid "30c57b85-780d-5e2f-88d6-2b0bf8507810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557967} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2c83f9-30fa-58a9-ab6d-b815a4faa3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558075} {:answer/id #uuid "978ea838-5cf8-51dc-9cc3-827714cd57ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558160} {:answer/id #uuid "fad0f84d-6ada-5fb9-b0e6-bd2a4abb6d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea7e0be-9a1f-5523-b787-ed5f453051d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557964} :answer-field/id #uuid "97da889e-de7b-5fe7-9f12-0a62150c1338" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e26325a0-a17c-5d3b-96e5-ffcb13cdecc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-107491" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{L}\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,\\underbrace{(LU)}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL\\underbrace{(Ux)}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-3 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-3$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e33c97-0499-5829-9886-be30b00989ae" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eea679e-1d00-5848-aa6b-11d4e2a5e9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558017} {:answer/id #uuid "86e0a1d5-1b21-502e-9724-c39fe8bedec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558131} {:answer/id #uuid "8f98a11a-a9f4-5967-826b-9561bcb1c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 50 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 58 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 62 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 65 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 70\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558147} {:answer/id #uuid "a34dfa2c-d0f7-5cbc-becb-9f788df746d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 1 \\\\ 12 & 2 \\\\ 15 & 3 \\\\ 20 & 4 \\\\ 17 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558191} {:answer/id #uuid "a9ffd8b7-b5cd-5adc-9457-bfa1bef7fd01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f98a11a-a9f4-5967-826b-9561bcb1c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 50 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 58 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 62 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 65 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 70\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558147} :answer-field/id #uuid "d12fb1e1-1778-564e-b514-5a394648ba52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe25ae24-c60e-57ec-8c52-078b3a7606de" :question/math-academy-id "q-139864" :question/problem "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$50$** | **$58$** | **$62$** | **$65$** | **$70$** |\n| $y$ | $10$ | $12$ | $15$ | $20$ | $17$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the plane $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$50$** | **$58$** | **$62$** | **$65$** | **$70$** |\n| $y$ | $10$ | $12$ | $15$ | $20$ | $17$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 50 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 58 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 62 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 65 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 70\\end{aligned}]}^{X}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{\\beta } & =\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]}^{y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e8a9640-d5a2-5af9-85c3-9df541069e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560634} {:answer/id #uuid "8408d7f7-986c-53a7-8060-d0e712a043fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560641} {:answer/id #uuid "ac845e78-dfdf-51a2-9552-e2548a59f300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-3)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560710} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8b46c1-8a21-5eb2-9692-195052a1df74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560820} {:answer/id #uuid "f0444fa0-516b-5c9b-82d3-af49b3feedc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e8a9640-d5a2-5af9-85c3-9df541069e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560634} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7e4408-fbc9-5f18-bf91-1f672892b184" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8478761-1f4e-5c9d-a634-3425df7889e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124490" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(k-1)!$ for any $k\\ge 4?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have \n\n$$\n(k-1)!=(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)\\cdot (k-4)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(k-1)! & =(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot \\overbrace{(k-3)\\cdot (k-4)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}^{(k-3)!} \\\\  & =(k-1)\\cdot (k-2)\\cdot (k-3)!\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b049dea4-5045-57ec-ad6a-c49f30e5da1f" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Matrix to Rotation-Scaling Form Given Multiple Parts of the Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12fab1be-92c3-5c73-9057-2ce01cfa87cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561641} {:answer/id #uuid "1b236a4d-fc2f-53b6-af86-4c4f9793792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561656} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca133f2-63fd-5e30-bf07-bb0ae8d8988a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561777} {:answer/id #uuid "66b397cb-7b81-5983-a6b0-49e027e16f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561836} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5d726b-4c91-5de1-b99c-cbf38e533e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12fab1be-92c3-5c73-9057-2ce01cfa87cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561641} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fea878e-a991-5b88-82fa-0dff5d838738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fed17ade-b98f-5b7e-aa56-3747d2eae8ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-99343" :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-4+3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3-2\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}\\underbrace{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c68664c1-bc59-51c1-932c-d6f7c8476470" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of a Vector Function Using Properties of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04142752-c01a-5e11-89a6-6b5adc4ed5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-2,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562945} {:answer/id #uuid "21d9e57e-bfa3-586e-9b91-d4dc21a2545d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563020} {:answer/id #uuid "24d7bfc2-51e1-5033-adbd-48343a267821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,0,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563028} {:answer/id #uuid "2918dce8-4f46-5431-aa05-6401af531bcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563037} {:answer/id #uuid "caef0b1a-9245-5da8-b22a-8dda3c23c0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,1,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24d7bfc2-51e1-5033-adbd-48343a267821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,0,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563028} :answer-field/id #uuid "88941887-29dc-54a4-8201-4203e16bb84e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05950ac2-f758-5682-b193-f12241b0a085" :question/math-academy-id "q-127820" :question/problem "Find $f(5)$ given that  $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are two continuous vector-valued functions for which   $g(5)=⟨-1,1,-2⟩$ and \n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 5}[f(t)+3g(t)]=⟨1,3,1⟩\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the  addition rule for limits, and the fact that both functions are continuous, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 5}[f(t)+3g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 5}f(t)+{lim}_{t\\to 5}[3g(t)] \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to 5}f(t)+3{lim}_{t\\to 5}g(t) \\\\  & =f(5)+3g(5) \\\\  & =f(5)+3\\underbrace{⟨-1,1,-2⟩}_{g(5)} \\\\  & =f(5)+⟨-3,3,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, we are told that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 5}[f(t)+3g(t)]=⟨1,3,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain the following equation which we can solve for $f(5):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 5}[f(t)+3g(t)] & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ f(5)+⟨-3,3,-6⟩ & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ f(5) & =⟨1,3,1⟩-⟨-3,3,-6⟩ \\\\ f(5) & =⟨4,0,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c68664c1-bc59-51c1-932c-d6f7c8476470" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of a Vector Function Using Properties of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44b00ccb-8b01-596c-b4dc-2a3f3aa5a049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-3,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563099} {:answer/id #uuid "45c07133-7c78-580f-9ccc-4af3dc31a4d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of $f(0)$ cannot be determined." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563102} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea82692-100a-5038-b8d4-644562b66a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563267} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1f037b-158b-5c79-8e25-3276bfa998c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563399} {:answer/id #uuid "f107cc53-ee96-570c-9ee3-a5f4ee8def54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f107cc53-ee96-570c-9ee3-a5f4ee8def54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563483} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fe35960-523d-5648-9c8e-2980e2ae45c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56eb1f68-e0b0-5d8c-82fe-65522b38bb34" :question/math-academy-id "q-35115" :question/problem "Find $f(0)$ given that  $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are two continuous vector-valued functions for which   $g(0)=⟨-1,0,1⟩$ and \n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)-g(t)]=⟨-2,-3,0⟩\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the  addition rule for limits, and the fact that both functions are continuous, we get:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)-g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)+{lim}_{t\\to 0}[-g(t)] \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =f(0)-g(0) \\\\  & =f(0)-\\underbrace{⟨-1,0,1⟩}_{g(0)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, we are told that:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)-g(t)]=⟨-2,-3,0⟩\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain the following equation which we can solve for $f(0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)-g(t)] & =⟨-2,-3,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2,-3,0⟩ & =f(0)-⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2,-3,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩ & =f(0) \\\\ f(0) & =⟨-3,-3,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58e2e40e-209b-5bc7-98df-11841c2bbcc3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment With Variable Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13df7405-37a9-5376-a794-b50ade14b257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563997} {:answer/id #uuid "2248598d-8d45-5b33-a1bb-161e7e022f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2p,-4q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564017} {:answer/id #uuid "41743567-93b3-52b5-956f-5e3cf584ae66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564079} {:answer/id #uuid "b2dfc1f4-7244-51d1-b08e-beaf085cffe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564249} {:answer/id #uuid "cd30a56d-8702-5fad-b81c-b55db3829574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4p,-2q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2dfc1f4-7244-51d1-b08e-beaf085cffe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564249} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c69590-b35f-5b4e-b1cf-478ea7e99763" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a0af22d-5fcd-5a62-b138-4a5969bb9fc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73730" :question/problem "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(8p,-q)$ and $(-2p,-9q).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between $\\underbrace{(8p,-q)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and $\\underbrace{(-2p,-9q)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8p+(-2p)}{2},\\frac{-q+(-9q)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8p-2p}{2},\\frac{-q-9q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{6p}{2},\\frac{-10q}{2}) \\\\  & =(3p,-5q).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d177b305-cdd1-5f91-b9d5-90623e52ad10" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System Given a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e9e21c3-28d7-5744-b751-8735eef80c3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564048} {:answer/id #uuid "45ccbd17-a611-5e51-8f96-c134314902f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564085} {:answer/id #uuid "6c912a39-aa9c-5584-bd27-ebb5f9b76c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564139} {:answer/id #uuid "8c06bd3e-d522-582e-8e6e-842930f9ae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564186} {:answer/id #uuid "ae08b2e2-ed79-5464-95a9-3d40e4f6d24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c06bd3e-d522-582e-8e6e-842930f9ae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564186} :answer-field/id #uuid "99733e29-1d7e-5770-81f4-dc925a89eb32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0061631-6269-58a0-a054-4e33a330ba6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-139798" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{R}x & =\\overbrace{\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}]}^{{Q}^{T}}\\overbrace{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}^{b} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}9{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{2}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=9.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}_{1}+8(9) & =-9 \\\\ 9{x}_{1} & =-81 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58e2e40e-209b-5bc7-98df-11841c2bbcc3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment With Variable Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b86450-d396-50c2-b792-96eb2e069dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-w,-z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563969} {:answer/id #uuid "1707b2e5-7f13-581b-928d-cb954858885d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2w,2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563999} {:answer/id #uuid "2295ae60-1e26-5128-8f27-466b06ffd6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2w,3z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564018} {:answer/id #uuid "2c117928-80a8-595c-9b86-d8c72d7f0afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2w,-2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564039} {:answer/id #uuid "c0661565-ff3d-5e5e-b035-22e247858f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-w,2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1707b2e5-7f13-581b-928d-cb954858885d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2w,2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563999} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c637ca-477b-51e8-ad73-42e7989eff3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f548e29c-4fb0-5de0-8aa0-2659faa5a2eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73720" :question/problem "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-w,7z)$ and $(5w,-3z).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between $\\underbrace{(-w,7z)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and $\\underbrace{(5w,-3z)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-w+5w}{2},\\frac{7z+(-3z)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-w+5w}{2},\\frac{7z-3z}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4w}{2},\\frac{4z}{2}) \\\\  & =(2w,2z).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e69b24-bdab-519d-9db4-fa9f763bec4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564969} {:answer/id #uuid "40a41c4a-74f2-5a0d-80b4-6255b626fcc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565033} {:answer/id #uuid "577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565072} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ad3c78-1256-5dff-9d91-4d2324618c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∧R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565203} {:answer/id #uuid "f27b8716-005f-5b70-a4d1-fcf5671b7cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2accb16-6316-5d25-b406-7af92337b373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df" :question/math-academy-id "q-177452" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}$ is rational, **or** $3|12$ **and** $3|18.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $Q:3|12$\n\n- $R:3|18\\text{ }$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\sqrt{5}$ is rational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3|12$ and $3|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{3|12}_{Q}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{3|18}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∧R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{3|12\\text{ and }3|18}_{Q\\,∧\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∧R).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565035} {:answer/id #uuid "56b8008e-3e0e-50d5-b98d-6f1ae9548a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565035} :answer-field/id #uuid "1de9cdf1-94b6-56c2-bf7d-3647210da7b1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564958} {:answer/id #uuid "addf42f9-b92a-50aa-840e-9cebd676a066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564958} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6f16fd-3b2c-5aaa-8d4b-bff5822eb1f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cde20091-5ea0-5e89-8e56-3c6da49f96e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565246} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565311} :answer-field/id #uuid "c48b5f22-688c-554b-b977-496452316b1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489" :question/math-academy-id "q-178163" :question/problem "$$\n\\underbrace{0\\text{ is even}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{\\overbrace{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{1\\}=\\{1,2\\}}^{Q}\\,\\overbrace{\\text{or}}^{∨}\\,\\overbrace{\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ is irrational}}^{R}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∨(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, but the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∨\\overbrace{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}^{\\text{false}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3286434a-593f-5cc4-acfc-6bb0f2812c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569516} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6682e2-223f-5551-9555-606e0dc281da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569547} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb0dc58-f354-538c-8aef-2413ca8d7f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569648} {:answer/id #uuid "97984476-2d2e-53cd-84f2-a709077ec7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569683} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2156fb-e1ff-51c3-b81e-f5cafa615c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97984476-2d2e-53cd-84f2-a709077ec7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569683} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9382a07-3a03-5be2-b528-235df29742b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14def4d3-3d45-5610-862f-8d4c651f0955" :question/math-academy-id "q-106760" :question/problem "Given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 10\\end{bmatrix}$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & \\,{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{{E}_{1}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{L}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60d81581-c221-5494-a432-08d979f7a43d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569593} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca3072c-d6ac-5918-a623-20411f8b7700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569647} {:answer/id #uuid "acfff4be-1f46-5b1f-a60f-b1bb756a3b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569714} {:answer/id #uuid "fb15c2de-88fd-5d61-a019-1eb95f578d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569838} {:answer/id #uuid "fba3dcfb-a5b2-547c-8691-6e722e502046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb15c2de-88fd-5d61-a019-1eb95f578d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569838} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1d1148-bcd2-52a8-8f81-b71b67b2ffca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66c0358e-dcf2-5965-acb4-eb43f1da9799" :question/math-academy-id "q-74951" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{{E}_{1}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{L}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17429e2c-6a7d-5799-9f99-11411731d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569478} {:answer/id #uuid "3cbd73d2-cd1b-5b1f-b775-9c124c82a91b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569526} {:answer/id #uuid "4d58d8e8-ebbf-5227-901f-b377591464ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569550} {:answer/id #uuid "9a8638fd-45d4-525e-afd5-446d9bab6953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569689} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdfcc6c-043a-5b9e-8a4c-0bfab8faa665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d58d8e8-ebbf-5227-901f-b377591464ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569550} :answer-field/id #uuid "808d2fc9-2e7f-5ef1-86ff-cfcf9e8e2abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "903883c2-c07e-50f2-a202-1c38e08cadfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-32550" :question/problem "Given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$ has the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{{E}_{1}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{L}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdded031-fd95-5a7f-92d4-c0d6713ba64d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfccf1a2-81a4-586f-b6af-2f70838ec300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfccf1a2-81a4-586f-b6af-2f70838ec300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571939} :answer-field/id #uuid "13d56c94-2d25-54b7-b65c-c2ab11270b92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18f21b66-7036-5909-982a-f6e8c6a583c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-216300" :question/problem "The distance between the points $(5,1)$ and $(1,-2)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have $\\underbrace{(5,1)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and $\\underbrace{(1,-2)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$ \nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-5)^{2}+(-2-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "379919fe-14c5-5033-9b3a-c01fc06e063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571636} {:answer/id #uuid "52c6b9cc-ce8b-5b07-bd83-778a557af4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571689} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3f86e3-aa37-529d-833c-43163e45c374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571779} {:answer/id #uuid "92676a16-1339-55d9-9df9-b454ed1dd9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571797} {:answer/id #uuid "dcfb51fc-582b-51c5-801a-8eebb92fb524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92676a16-1339-55d9-9df9-b454ed1dd9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571797} :answer-field/id #uuid "99558049-622d-5685-b782-575ef24f9379" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "410f5e90-695f-5bc0-8245-a684010c1ba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-119112" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d939db899518bec1c91fd70e4d16726ec7a12d32f2d7b41575759843e5837d6c.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$" :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $\\underbrace{(-1,1)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and $\\underbrace{(3,-2)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-(-1))^{2}+(-2-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572130 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78183e78-e617-5692-8a7d-a04e6565cbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78183e78-e617-5692-8a7d-a04e6565cbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571744} :answer-field/id #uuid "b282633f-0ee1-506a-a430-4ffd87e35c4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c32c57d-e2a6-5951-aed3-798fe23141b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-216289" :question/problem "![](images/92/923997b18a24320bab5eb7ca39dc04d7da52e10ebf18ff4cb7f8ec40bf00b491.png)\n\nThe length of $\\overset{―}{CD}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $C$ and $D$ have coordinates $\\underbrace{(7,1)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and $\\underbrace{(1,9)}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively. \n\nTo find the distance $CD,$ we can use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-7)^{2}+(9-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129214 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f3ba21-6407-503e-aec0-fa4462a69e73" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Matrix to Rotation-Scaling Form Using the Complex Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27fcac0c-32b4-50b7-a320-2ac89d925ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571606} {:answer/id #uuid "39c17d8b-7383-565d-82ff-9034e842313a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571643} {:answer/id #uuid "894dd0ee-996e-5946-926e-1667d9661d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571774} {:answer/id #uuid "a5514041-c574-508e-9c48-296d90937fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571825} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a5c562-7c09-52ed-9124-62137601a6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27fcac0c-32b4-50b7-a320-2ac89d925ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571606} :answer-field/id #uuid "621d2560-2a88-546c-aa01-9273b93c0401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80ffb1ef-2b1d-5387-91a1-65dcd637622b" :question/math-academy-id "q-99410" :question/problem "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2-5\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=2+5\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172028 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26871e46-51ca-5680-a064-bcee4ac984fd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Curve Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52c08f07-4189-509a-b220-5216f042453d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572415} {:answer/id #uuid "8635fe6e-fac6-55c1-996c-c85b1599c832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An circle of radius $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572461} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d80198-d0f9-5a4a-bda4-ee01da631e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{3}$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572491} {:answer/id #uuid "a5629f9b-9362-5ae4-8c5b-612ef5f66982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A pair of intersecting lines" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572493} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3f94a7-6795-5611-8617-8bdcc199a8ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabola" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5629f9b-9362-5ae4-8c5b-612ef5f66982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A pair of intersecting lines" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572493} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a95532-8eb9-58d2-950f-597816548f39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "13426e81-09a1-5f21-879b-4654e3684393" :question/math-academy-id "q-95398" :question/problem "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2},$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note the following:\n\n$$\nC:\\,\\underbrace{{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}}_{Q(x)}+2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2\n$$\n\nLet's write the given change of variables explicitly:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe know that the given change of variables reduces $Q(x)$ to its canonical form. Therefore, performing the change of variables on $C,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2})-2(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2} & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}-2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for the variable ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}-2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2} & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-({y}_{2}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-({y}_{2}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}-(\\sqrt{2})^{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-({y}_{2}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}+2-2) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{({y}_{2}+\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+2 & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{({y}_{2}+\\sqrt{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{z}_{1} &={y}_{1}, \\\\ {z}_{2} &={y}_{2}+\\sqrt{2},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{2}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the pair of intersecting lines ${z}_{2}=\\sqrt{3}{z}_{1}$ and ${z}_{2}=-\\sqrt{3}{z}_{1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11730b49-5c1b-553f-a0cd-5065a0dc5199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574977} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3c59c9-503f-5ae0-b3a5-872155cbacb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧(B∨A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575056} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc95fc3-0584-51d0-a312-1cdf402e6d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575059} {:answer/id #uuid "63d24958-d529-55a1-bb97-dbc8287d4ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575130} {:answer/id #uuid "a1142e71-f01d-53db-85c7-f72b0e85cdc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d24958-d529-55a1-bb97-dbc8287d4ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575130} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0545d6-6269-5947-88bb-012e08cb4777" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c5b86f8-d52f-5a20-8d0d-0aaa46ba2066" :question/math-academy-id "q-170732" :question/problem "$x$ is a multiple of $3$ **or** negative.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $3$\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is negative" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is a multiple of 3}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is negative}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c5f076-2dad-57e5-86da-dcf767728159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧N)∨(U∧W)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575007} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa24a3b-0cf6-564d-bbd2-5ed0ad7d9580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(U∨W)∧(N∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575017} {:answer/id #uuid "544b3410-55a9-57b5-ab4a-a712e386d5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧W)∨(P∧U)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575096} {:answer/id #uuid "83370d52-ce6f-51ff-b890-36f3abdaa7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨W)∨(P∨U)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575184} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d89619-99fb-5b26-aa6a-eddccb7eb088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨W)∧(P∨U)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "544b3410-55a9-57b5-ab4a-a712e386d5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧W)∨(P∧U)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575096} :answer-field/id #uuid "2649b6c2-492e-5356-a831-8263ce9a3a65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b324032-316f-5d2c-a64e-c71b992cc557" :question/math-academy-id "q-170744" :question/problem "$x$ is negative **and** irrational, **or** $x$ is positive **and** less than $5.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\n- $W(x):$ $x$ is irrational\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $U(x):$ $x$ is less than $5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative and irrational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is negative}}_{N}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is irrational}}_{W},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∧W.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive and less than $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is positive }}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is less than }5}_{U},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧U.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is negative and irrational}}_{N∧W}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is positive and less than }5}_{P∧U},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∧W)∨(P∧U).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc6846f-da86-5edc-8197-5dd6ab0d515b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N∨I∨G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575031} {:answer/id #uuid "3a990b3b-e50c-55f4-841c-48540a89bea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨I)∧(N∨G)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575048} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4cdf67-55da-5845-afc2-158e6ab7917e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨I)∧G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575111} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ae40aa-e0c5-5ecd-993e-b28f6b3e0dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N∧(I∨G)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575360} {:answer/id #uuid "fd90d54e-01f7-575a-a1ce-e4adcea956f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N∧I∧G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fc6846f-da86-5edc-8197-5dd6ab0d515b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N∨I∨G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575031} :answer-field/id #uuid "86923f36-2336-5931-98c5-4bc40ad3f1a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf7bd3ae-1af0-5d1c-98ba-75865a7d1ce0" :question/math-academy-id "q-175379" :question/problem "$x$ is negative **or** an integer, **or** $x$ is greater than $4.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\n- $I(x):$ $x$ is an integer\n\n- $G(x):$ $x$ is greater than $4$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative or an integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is negative}}_{N}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is an integer }}_{I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨I.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is greater than $4.$ This corresponds to $G.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is negative or an integer }}_{N∨I}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is greater than }4}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨I∨G.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2831f9-56d4-5d26-b2d1-8c3127c9f5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(L∨O)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575018} {:answer/id #uuid "452d777d-7cc1-590f-b684-a0da89c9b7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧L)∨O" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575071} {:answer/id #uuid "7f61874f-0b6a-5d57-af59-98cf5c43faea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨L∨O" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575179} {:answer/id #uuid "a3ee7079-fd3c-5328-92cb-17dcbcb9c236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧L∧O" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575238} {:answer/id #uuid "d5975a4d-0efb-50bd-ae9f-843c27623fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(L∧O)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3ee7079-fd3c-5328-92cb-17dcbcb9c236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧L∧O" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575238} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6828370-b586-53a4-8e88-116bcad7ec85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da39f028-b35d-56a8-9983-4818944cc5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-175382" :question/problem "$x$ is a prime **and** less than $15$, **and** $x$ is odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is prime\n\n- $L(x):$ $x$ is less than $15$\n\n- $O(x):$ $x$ is odd" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:**  $x$ is a prime and less than $15.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is prime}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is less than }15}_{L},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧L.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is odd. This corresponds to $O.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is a prime and less than }15}_{P∧L}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is odd }}_{O},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧L∧O.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18c6b864-ec7f-507b-a1d6-37aaf7109761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574989} {:answer/id #uuid "3f48ff9c-4f28-58c3-8057-031c97ce17cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575057} {:answer/id #uuid "70090cfa-39e0-535c-97ba-4e7cc9a1fe00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575153} {:answer/id #uuid "a66a4923-5edc-5e09-90ef-eec31f5cf445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575240} {:answer/id #uuid "ae05cfac-91fd-526f-a243-a17648420ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70090cfa-39e0-535c-97ba-4e7cc9a1fe00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575153} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3382ac5-0ab3-59c9-ab02-9b04f3ae190e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e879e661-bcef-55f1-b1d6-53b6386bc86f" :question/math-academy-id "q-175347" :question/problem "$x$ is odd **and** a multiple of $3.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $3$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is odd}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is a multiple of }3}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575626 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c69ab7e-fdc4-577a-afc4-5efc1c8da77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∨(G∧H)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575113} {:answer/id #uuid "76dd5f9c-6749-54d9-8fc6-d3fec5efe88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∧(G∨H)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575168} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ea5ef2-3ada-54f7-969b-3198aafa6288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(F∧G)∧H" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575245} {:answer/id #uuid "addc3908-57ac-54ed-883f-425294653323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(F∨G)∧H" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575257} {:answer/id #uuid "f75427e7-171a-5d90-be71-724fefa93612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(F∧G)∨H" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f75427e7-171a-5d90-be71-724fefa93612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(F∧G)∨H" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575388} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3de54ca-72e7-5a7f-8abc-16424ae427df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff367501-0855-59a2-85d9-edfbeeaeb047" :question/math-academy-id "q-170746" :question/problem "$x$ is greater than $10$ **and** prime, **or** $x$ is negative.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $F(x):$ $x$ is greater than $10$\n\n- $G(x):$ $x$ is prime\n\n- $H(x):$ $x$ is negative" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is greater than $10$ and prime. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{is greater than}\\,10}_{F}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is prime}}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $F∧G.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is negative. This corresponds to $H.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\,\\text{ is greater than}\\,10\\,\\text{and prime}}_{F∧G}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is negative}}_{H},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(F∧G)∨H.$"}]}
